.\" groff man page for the Basic Next REPL executable (0.6 line).
.TH BNR 1 "October 25, 2026" "bnr 0.6.8" "Basic Next"
.SH NAME
bnr \- Basic Next interactive Read-Eval-Print Loop (REPL)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bnr
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ file.bn ]
.RI [ "-- program-args" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bnr
is the interactive Read-Eval-Print Loop (REPL) companion for Basic Next.
It allows incremental entry and evaluation of Basic Next expressions, variable bindings,
functions, types, and statements, preserving memory state, ARC references, and declared
symbols across turns without re-executing history.
.PP
Unlike batch mode in
.BR bni (1)
or compilation in
.BR bnc (1),
statements and expressions entered at the
.B bnr>
prompt do not require an enclosing
.BR "FUNCTION Start" .
Multi-line constructs (such as
.BR IF ,
.BR FOR ,
.BR WHILE ,
.BR FUNCTION ,
or
.BR CLASS )
automatically switch the prompt to
.B ...>
until the construct is closed.
.SH META-COMMANDS
The following interactive commands begin with a colon:
.TP
.B :help
Display summary of REPL commands, options, and keyboard shortcuts.
.TP
.BR :quit ", " :q
Exit the REPL session cleanly.
.TP
.B :reset
Reset all accumulated session bindings, types, and variables, maintaining the initial security policy.
.TP
.BR :bindings ", " :vars
List all active variables, types, and their ARC memory status.
.TP
.BI :type " expr"
Resolve and display the static type of an expression in the current session context without executing it.
.TP
.B :policy
Display the effective execution policy and security sandbox configuration.
.TP
.BI :load " file.bn"
Load and execute declarations from the specified Basic Next source file into the active session.
.TP
.BI :arc " [binding]"
Inspect ARC memory state, active object reference counts, and subsystem native handles.
.TP
.BI :ir " [expr|func]"
Display the validated BN IR intermediate representation for an expression or the accumulated session.
.TP
.BI :cfg " [func]"
Display control flow graph basic blocks and terminator instructions.
.TP
.BI :bench " expr"
Benchmark the given expression across multiple iterations and report execution times alongside ARC memory allocation deltas.
.TP
.BI :doc " symbol"
Display signature and member documentation for the specified symbol, module, or HOST capability.
.TP
.BI :export " file.bn"
Export all accumulated valid session declarations and bindings into a canonical Basic Next program suitable for bni check and bnc native compilation.
.TP
.B :clear
Clear the terminal screen.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Ctrl-C
Discard current multi-line input buffer during collection, or cancel currently running evaluation.
.TP
.B Ctrl-D
Exit the REPL when pressed on an empty line.
.TP
.B Ctrl-R
Reverse search through command history.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --no-filesystem
Deny access to
.BR HOST.FileSystem
and related filesystem operations.
.TP
.BI --ffi-path " dir"
Add an ordered dynamic library search directory for FFI resolution (repeatable).
.TP
.BR -v , " --verbose"
Show pipeline stages (repeat for token stream output: -v -v).
.TP
.BI --module-path " dir"
Add an ordered import search directory (repeatable).
.TP
.B --sandbox
Opt into filesystem root restrictions.
.TP
.BI --read-root " dir"
Allow filesystem reads below a sandbox root (repeatable).
.TP
.BI --write-root " dir"
Allow filesystem writes below a sandbox root (repeatable).
.TP
.B --warnings errors
Promote all warning diagnostics to errors.
.TP
.BI --allow " CODE"
Suppress one warning diagnostic (repeatable).
.TP
.BI --warn " CODE"
Keep one warning diagnostic at warning level.
.TP
.BI --deny " CODE"
Promote one warning diagnostic to an error.
.TP
.BI --color " auto|always|never"
Control ANSI color styling on diagnostics and status messages.
.TP
.BI --log-level " error|warn|info|debug"
Process log verbosity level.
.TP
.BI --log-file " file"
Companion process log file path.
.TP
.B --no-log
Disable companion process logging.
.TP
.BI --config " file"
Load warning and logging configuration file.
.TP
.BR -V , " --version"
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print help text and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BNR_HISTORY_FILE
Override default path for command history file (defaults to
.IR ~/.bn_history ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bni (1),
.BR bnc (1)
.PP
Tutorial book: https://github.com/cquintella/basicnext-book
